        "| Empirical distribution | $\\hat p\\in\\Delta^{d-1}$ | token frequency distribution |\n",
        "\n",
        "## Common misconceptions\n",
        "\n",
        "### Misconception 1: tokenization is just cleaning\n",
        "\n",
        "Tokenization is not just cleaning.  It defines the symbols used by the model.  It changes the statistical problem.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Misconception 2: words are the natural tokens\n",
        "\n",
        "Words are intuitive for humans, but they are not always the best modeling units.  Subwords often provide better coverage and a more stable vocabulary.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Misconception 3: larger vocabulary is always better\n",
        "\n",
        "A larger vocabulary can represent more distinctions, but it also creates a higher-dimensional and sparser estimation problem.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Misconception 4: one-hot vectors encode meaning\n",
        "\n",
        "One-hot vectors encode identity, not meaning.  Meaning enters later through co-occurrence, embeddings, attention, and learned model parameters.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Worked exercise: comparing tokenizers\n",
